{"units": [{"id": "lego-quote182", "translation": "telling some to do one thing, others to do nothing"}, {"id": "lego-quote183", "translation": "and the rest I bid him to oversee here"}, {"id": "lego-quote184", "translation": "I say that unjust things should not prevail by oaths"}, {"id": "lego-quote185", "translation": "I bid this concern be put aside"}, {"id": "lego-quote186", "translation": "and I tell you in all: revere the altar of Justice"}, {"id": "lego-quote187", "translation": "I mean the thief of fire"}, {"id": "lego-quote188", "translation": "I mean the circle of the shield"}, {"id": "lego-quote189", "translation": "I mean the son of Oecles"}, {"id": "lego-quote190", "translation": "I mean Polyneices"}, {"id": "lego-quote191", "translation": "I mean Cassandra"}, {"id": "lego-quote192", "translation": "I mean Electra"}, {"id": "lego-quote193", "translation": "I mean you"}, {"id": "lego-quote194", "translation": "I mean the scorpion's dart"}, {"id": "lego-quote195", "translation": "I mean your mother"}, {"id": "lego-quote196", "translation": "for great indeed he speaks by the throne of Zeus (M reads λέγῃ)"}, {"id": "lego-quote197", "translation": "greater than what was said before"}, {"id": "lego-quote198", "translation": "brother of the one mentioned before"}, {"id": "lego-quote199", "translation": "do you have anything apart from what has been said?"}, {"id": "lego-quote200", "translation": "since enough has been said"}, {"id": "lego-word1", "translation": "of words"}, {"id": "lego-word2", "translation": "would say nothing"}, {"id": "lego-word3", "translation": "nor will he speak before..."}, {"id": "lego-word4", "translation": "whom"}, {"id": "lego-word5", "translation": "as"}, {"id": "lego-word6", "translation": "you say"}, {"id": "lego-word7", "translation": "you might say"}, {"id": "lego-word8", "translation": "having licked"}, {"id": "lego-word9", "translation": "for I do not speak of Aegisthus' death"}, {"id": "lego-word10", "translation": "I say"}, {"id": "lego-word11", "translation": "I blame"}, {"id": "lego-word12", "translation": "towards"}, {"id": "lego-word13", "translation": "saying"}, {"id": "lego-word14", "translation": "I"}, {"id": "lego-word15", "translation": "I say"}, {"id": "lego-word16", "translation": "I say"}, {"id": "lego-word17", "translation": "I am called"}, {"id": "lego-word18", "translation": "will be said"}, {"id": "lego-word19", "translation": "to say"}, {"id": "lego-word20", "translation": "to those who have been spoken to"}, {"id": "lego-word21", "translation": "in conversations"}, {"id": "lego-word22", "translation": "conversation"}, {"id": "leibo-orth1", "translation": "to pour, to drip"}, {"id": "leibo-def1", "translation": "to pour, to drip"}, {"id": "leibo-def2", "translation": "to pour a libation"}, {"id": "leibo-note1", "translation": "Of tears, a usage frequent in Homer and others, on which see Thes. vol. 5 p. 159."}, {"id": "leibo-note2", "translation": "λειβομένα [dripping] is corrupt from δ' εἰβομ εἰβομένα: See under εἴβομαι."}, {"id": "leibo-quote1", "translation": "shedding tears"}, {"id": "leibo-quote2", "translation": "and from their eyes they drip a hateful stream"}, {"id": "leibo-quote3", "translation": "the Argives must pray and sacrifice and pour libations"}, {"id": "leibo-word1", "translation": "dripping"}, {"id": "leibo-word2", "translation": "δ' εἰβομ εἰβομένα"}, {"id": "leibo-word3", "translation": "to be poured"}, {"id": "leimon-orth1", "translation": "meadow"}, {"id": "leimon-def1", "translation": "meadow"}, {"id": "leimon-quote1", "translation": "to the deep meadow of Lerna"}, {"id": "leimon-quote2", "translation": "a meadow rich in cattle"}, {"id": "leimon-quote3", "translation": "a snow-fed meadow"}, {"id": "leimonios-orth1", "translation": "of the meadow"}, {"id": "leimonios-def1", "translation": "of the meadow"}, {"id": "leimonios-quote1", "translation": "meadow dews"}, {"id": "leimonios-quote2", "translation": "meadow flowers"}, {"id": "leios-orth1", "translation": "smooth"}, {"id": "leios-def1", "translation": "smooth"}, {"id": "leios-note1", "translation": "Improperly of bland speech."}, {"id": "leios-quote1", "translation": "they soothed with smooth words"}, {"id": "leiotes-orth1", "translation": "smoothness"}, {"id": "leiotes-def1", "translation": "smoothness"}, {"id": "leiotes-quote1", "translation": "and what smoothness of entrails and what color would they have for the pleasure of the gods"}, {"id": "leipo-orth1", "translation": "to leave, to abandon"}, {"id": "leipo-def1", "translation": "to leave, to abandon"}, {"id": "leipo-def2", "translation": "Passive λείπομαι: to be left behind"}, {"id": "leipo-def3", "translation": "to be left, to remain"}, {"id": "leipo-def4", "translation": "to be defeated, to be inferior"}, {"id": "leipo-note1", "translation": "τὴν πόλιν [the city], which is understood from τάνδε πόλιν [this city] that follows. Schol.: μηδέποτε ἐπὶ τοῦ ἐμοῦ βίου καταλείποιεν τὴν πόλιν οἱ θεοί [may the gods never abandon the city during my lifetime]."}, {"id": "leipo-note2", "translation": "Ἀγβάτανα λιπών [having left Ecbatana], where προλιπών [having left behind] is restored from the copies."}, {"id": "leipo-quote1", "translation": "leaving the stream that bears his name"}, {"id": "leipo-quote2", "translation": "whom you must boldly leave and cross the Maeotic vale"}, {"id": "leipo-quote3", "translation": "and leaving the land of Europe"}, {"id": "leipo-quote4", "translation": "and they left them to be allotted"}, {"id": "leipo-quote5", "translation": "leaving the camp"}, {"id": "leipo-quote6", "translation": "may this assembly of gods never leave my life"}, {"id": "leipo-quote7", "translation": "leaving, I come to the gold-adorned halls"}, {"id": "leipo-quote8", "translation": "where did you leave these?"}, {"id": "leipo-quote9", "translation": "the chosen multitude of the army is left"}, {"id": "leipo-quote10", "translation": "you left Oebares, you left him"}, {"id": "leipo-quote11", "translation": "and leaving to the citizens shieldless tumults"}, {"id": "leipo-quote12", "translation": "such as she left"}, {"id": "leipo-quote13", "translation": "and the gold-embroidered halls – leaving"}, {"id": "leipo-quote14", "translation": "leaving this wagon-borne throne"}, {"id": "leipo-quote15", "translation": "leaving the newly captured city"}, {"id": "leipo-quote16", "translation": "leaving behind glory in the house"}, {"id": "leipo-quote17", "translation": "leaving these reports"}, {"id": "leipo-quote18", "translation": "and leaving the lake"}, {"id": "leipo-quote19", "translation": "that man I will never leave (thus Porson for λείπω)"}, {"id": "leipo-quote20", "translation": "and leaving the land of Dia, we flee to Syria with its common pasture"}, {"id": "leipo-quote21", "translation": "how did you dare to leave your ancestral home?"}, {"id": "leipo-quote22", "translation": "leave his branches"}, {"id": "leipo-quote23", "translation": "and now I leave them"}, {"id": "leipo-quote24", "translation": "leave the seats"}, {"id": "leipo-quote25", "translation": "do not leave wine-jars or water-jars in wealthy houses"}, {"id": "leipo-quote26", "translation": "for it is fated that you leave your weapons here"}, {"id": "leipo-quote27", "translation": "having sent away her bedmate, she is left alone"}, {"id": "leipo-quote28", "translation": "the leaders of the ships that were left"}, {"id": "leipo-quote29", "translation": "to receive the army left from the spear"}, {"id": "leipo-quote30", "translation": "hawks not far behind the doves"}, {"id": "leipo-quote31", "translation": "for the contest does not await men who are left behind"}]}